        "medication_code": "unknown",
        "dose": "standard"
      },
      "justification": "Patient presents with cough, fever, and dyspnea consistent with community-acquired pneumonia. Diagnostic workup has been initiated (CBC, BMP, chest X-ray, cultures, procalcitonin, CURB-65, Legionella antigen). IDSA/ATS CAP guidelines recommend empiric beta-lactam plus macrolide combination therapy for CAP requiring hospitalization. Vitals are currently stable but early antibiotic administration improves outcomes in pneumonia."
    },
    {
      "action_id": "give_respiratory_fluoroquinolone",
      "timestamp_minutes": 60.0,
      "type": "give_medication",
      "args": {
        "medication_code": "unknown",
        "dose": "standard"
      },
      "justification": "Patient presents with cough, fever, and dyspnea consistent with community-acquired pneumonia. A respiratory fluoroquinolone (e.g., levofloxacin or moxifloxacin) is an evidence-based alternative antibiotic regimen for CAP, providing broad coverage including atypical organisms. This is appropriate as an adjunct or alternative to the already-initiated beta-lactam plus macrolide regimen, particularly if there are concerns about atypical coverage or treatment response."
    },
    {
